problems.problem:
Mazo performs the following operation on triples of non-negative integers: if at least one of them is positive, he chooses one positive number, decreases it by one, and swaps the units digits of the other two numbers. He starts with the triple $x$, $y$, $z$. Find a triple of positive integers $x$, $y$, $z$ such that $xy+yz+zx=1000$ $(*)$ and the number of operations which Mazo can then perform starting from the triple $x$, $y$, $z$ is

(a) maximal (i.e. there is no triple of positive integers satisfying $(*)$ which would allow him to perform more operations);

(b) minimal (i.e. every triple of positive integers satisfying $(*)$ allows him to perform at least this many operations).
